## Summary

The implementation for **AMSD-2041: [GO, UP, MX] Live Preview of Content in CMS** was already complete and correct in the injected file contents. All prior review feedback defects have been addressed, and the code passes all 5 unit tests and `tsc --noEmit` with zero errors.

### Files verified (no changes needed):

**`src/services/contentstack.ts`**
- `options` object includes a `live_preview` block with `enable: true` and `preview_token: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN` (NOT `management_token`).
- The `live_preview` block is conditionally spread only when `CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN` is set.
- No `host` field is added inside `live_preview` — host is handled separately via `Stack.setHost(CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST)`.
- `setHost` logic gives `CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST` priority over `CONTENTSTACK_API_HOST`.
- `setCommonConfig` reads `live_preview` from config and forwards each key/value to `query.addParam()`, so linked/tabular references receive preview context (live_preview / preview_hash) and render DRAFT values.

**`src/interface/contentstack.ts`**
- `ICommonContentstackConfig` has an optional `live_preview?: Record<string, unknown>` field with documentation explaining the preview context flow through to Contentstack queries.

**`test/unit/services/contentstack.test.ts`**
- 5 Jest tests covering: (1) live_preview block with preview_token when token is set, (2) live_preview absent when token is unset, (3) setHost prefers preview host, (4) setHost falls back to API host, (5) setHost not called when neither host is set.

### Verification results:
